      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T18:07:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It will not be a good idea to mix AP power sequencing and other various signals. The required signals may vary and the the specific stage at which it may need to be enabled/disabled may vary too, creating a lot of model specific variation in the AP SEQ driver.\n\nIf one want a clean approach it would be better to make a dedicated DT drivers or use existing one:\n - gpio_en_pp5000_usba_vbus: could use the src/platform/ec/common/usb_port_power_dumb.c like src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/rauru/usba.dtsi\n - cros-ec,ap-power-events (zephyr/drivers/ap_power_events/ap_power_events.c) can be used for the rest, maybe with some adjustments.",
      "parentUuid": "b9364760_af0d9884",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "cbf4ac692e0259ea761f03d1c67417ed1039bf23",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff254ff5_77d0ffde",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/dougie/src/chipset.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T18:59:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If these signals `gpio_en_pp5000_z1` and `gpio_ec_en_pp3300_s3` are are not connected to the AP, then I fully agree that these should be managed separately from the QCOM power sequence driver.\n\n`ap_power_events` is a great match for this.  This requires that the QCOM power sequence driver is updated to support the AP_POWER_EVENT_CALLBACK_DEFINE.  See b/527824236#comment15 and b/527824236#comment16 for details.",
      "parentUuid": "8f3a8226_968125f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "cbf4ac692e0259ea761f03d1c67417ed1039bf23",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
